		{"id":"5be96d12519cfefe","type":"group","x":-920,"y":-1840,"width":520,"height":180,"color":"2","label":"Triad code of this canvas"},
		{"id":"198109e5dca50552","type":"file","file":"Rules Library/Triad Codes/(Reference) Triad Codes Master.md","x":920,"y":-1514,"width":1060,"height":934,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"432d8eb44bc4c8a0","type":"text","text":"> [!tldr] **Triad Codes**\n> **Triad Codes** are a compact indexing standard for the campaign. They enable reliable organization and retrieval across all layers and categories.\n>\n> **Format:** `DDD-CCC-EEE-C`\n> - **DDD — Domain:** top‑level category\n> - **CCC — Collection:** subcategory within the domain\n> - **EEE — Element:** specific entry\n> - **C — Checksum:** single‑character verifier used by tooling to confirm the code is valid\n>\n> *Example:* `ARC-LOC-042-K` (illustrative)\n","x":-880,"y":-1540,"width":1120,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"2416367d745cec1c","type":"text","text":"TBD list:\n- Quantum computer decryption capability (decryption level 1, 2, 3 etc - rules upgrades etc)","x":-2188,"y":-1530,"width":688,"height":1335},
		{"id":"3d3cc0e5df0f558b","type":"text","text":"# Revival ruleset","x":60,"y":1000,"width":509,"height":120,"color":"2"},
