		{"id":"4a2656b0e6e79a1a","type":"file","file":"Campaign Resources/Direct Game Used Assets/Game Data/Rules Library/References/(Reference) 5e Baseline (SRD 5.1).md","x":920,"y":-360,"width":1060,"height":940,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"b0d2fa72b4ec4e81","type":"text","text":"# Standard D&D  5e ruleset","x":-454,"y":70,"width":509,"height":80,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"4eebb19c97c6ca04","type":"text","text":"> [!tldr] **5e Baseline (SRD 5.1)**\n> We **import/reference** standard **D&D 5e** as the core engine. This note anchors the baseline; it does **not** reproduce book text—use the **PHB / SRD 5.1** for full rules.\n>\n> **Core beats:**\n> - **d20 checks:** roll **d20 + ability mod (+ proficiency if trained)** vs DC; **Advantage/Disadvantage** = roll 2d20, keep higher/lower.\n> - **Combat turn:** **1 Action**, **movement**, optional **1 Bonus Action** (if a feature grants it), and **1 Reaction** per round.\n> - **Attacks & saves:** attacks use d20 + relevant ability (+ PB if proficient); saving throws use the listed ability (+ PB if proficient).\n> - **Spells, damage, conditions, rests:** **as written** in 5e.\n>\n> **Note:** Any campaign‑specific overlays/house rules live in separate notes; this baseline remains **vanilla 5e**.\n","x":-880,"y":-410,"width":1560,"height":430,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"98f9d13c0af334c9","type":"text","text":"# **Inventory system**","x":60,"y":3400,"width":509,"height":120,"color":"2"},
